      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FUSSY AS (2) resumes as the one to beat, with his South Australian Class 1 runs carrying enough depth for this and his record at around 1100m reading well. The latest Morphettville eighth was too plain to take literally as a peak, but he was respected in an open market and now starts for Ray Viney in a race that should be within reach if he returns in order. JOSEPH'S GLORY (6) is fitter third-up and comes out of a BM64 at this track where he was only beaten just over four lengths, with the 2kg claim adding to his case. DOLCE D'AMOUR (5) has the clearest last-start placing, a checked second at this venue in a BM64, and barrier 1 gives her a platform to be competitive fresh. AGGRESSIVE (4) has to rebound from two wide-margin defeats over longer trips, but the Katherine BM64 reference and the Kerry Petrick yard keep him in the place mix.",
